+**Pitfalls:**
+*   **Lamp Culling:** Lamps whose upper-bound contribution is below the visible threshold are skipped. The upper-bound contribution is calculated as $\pi/h$, where $h$ is the distance from the ray to the lamp center [S1].
+*   **Shadow Map Instability:** Low shadow map resolution or unstable shadow maps cause flickering during cone tracing when the camera moves. Stabilizing the shadow map (e.g., computing directional light position from the view camera) may leave voxels unfilled if the shadow map resolution is low or not fully utilized [S3].
 
